  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia granted $15 million to the International Finance Cooperation to implement the Vietnam Private Sector Development Partnership, which has a strong focus on facilitating and promoting private investments to actively advance climate mitigation and adaptation. Australian funding supported stakeholders to implement actions contributing to low-carbon pathways, improve climate adaptation and reduce disaster risks. Australia supported the application of the International Finance Corporation&#x2019;s Excellence in Design for Greater Efficiencies certification which measures energy-saving features, water conservation and materials with reduced embedded carbon in building construction. In 2023, 840,000 square metres of total building floor were designed in accordance with the standards &#x2013; projected to save 17,719 megawatt hours of energy annually and cut greenhouse gas emissions by roughly 18,050 tons of CO2 per year.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate adaptation, mitigation, environment and biodiversity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia granted funding to the IFC for implementation of the Viet Nam Private Sector Development Partnership (VPSDP) which has a strong focus on facilitating and promoting private investments to actively advance climate mitigation and adaptation. Australian funding supported different stakeholders to implement actions contributing to low-carbon pathway and also improving climate adaptation and reducing disaster risks. Australia supported application of IFC&#x2019;s Excellence in Design for Greater Efficiencies (EDGE) certification which measures energy-saving features, water conservation and materials with reduced embedded carbon in building construction (840,000sqm were designed in accordance with EDGE standards which are projected to save 17,719 MWh of energy annually and cut GHG by roughly 18,050 tons of CO2/year).  Australia supports delivery of training programs and workshops to improve understanding of stakeholders about climate and disaster risks in the construction sector, through which stakeholders could apply tools to identify, plan and mainstream adaptive actions in design and construction.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food security</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&#x2019;s partnership with the International Finance Corporation (IFC) helped improve food safety and reduce food loss in agriculture and food supply chains through technical advice and capacity building. This work contributes to decreasing greenhouse gas emissions from the agriculture sector, which accounts for 35% of Vietnam&#x2019;s emissions. The partnership provided in-depth advisory support to eight companies in the agriculture sector and held training session and workshops reaching 4,498 people (1,491 women) on best practices to minimise food loss across various food supply chains. One example was targeted training on breeding, genetic selection and technical solutions to staff of the BAF Agriculture company, a &#x201c;feed-farm-food&#x201d; meat producer. This helped the company apply new techniques to reduce the animal mortality rate and increase average growth rates to reduce food loss. BAF implemented a greenhouse gas emission reduction action plan, including emission reductions from food loss, expansion of biogas electricity and realisation of carbon credits</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&#x2019;s partnership with the International Finance Corporation (IFC) strengthened the inclusion settings for private sector partner, Primark, in their garment factories in Vietnam. IFC provided advisory and training to Primark Vietnam factories to implement a Respectful Workplaces initiative to promote women&apos;s talent and reduce violence and harassment at work. The endline survey (end 2024) showed a reduction in the percentage of employees who reported experiencing workplace harassment and violence from 34% (baseline) to 13% (endline). Across the 12 participating factories, there was found to be an increase in employees&#x2019; knowledge on workplace harassment and violence (100%), improved employee trust to report grievances (92%), more structured grievance mechanisms in which contact teams are better equipped to handle situations (92%), which contributed to the firm being seen as an Employer of Choice (92%). There was a reduction in the share of employees who reported they had considered leaving their job because of workplace violence and harassment (from 15% to 7%).</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate adaptation, mitigation, environment and biodiversity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&#x2019;s partnership with the International Finance Corporation (IFC) supported the Government of Vietnam with advisory work on policies to incentivise climate investment and products. In 2024, technical assistance activities to investors, builders and developers on green building business cases and green building technologies, led to approximately 2.2 million sqm flooring designed in accordance with IFC&#x2019;s Excellence in Design for Greater Efficiencies standards (EDGE). This project is projected on an annual basis to save 28,000 MWh of energy, reduce water usage by 1.4 million m3 and cut greenhouse gas emission by over 27,000 tons/year. The IFC&#x2019;s Building Resilience Index has supported three real estate clients to identify climate risks and implement actions to mitigate potential losses, valued at up to US$30 million.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
